--TEST--
a session record may not live in the per-core tier, so the store a request on one core wrote is the store a request on another core reads — `rule:concurrency/the-local-tier-cannot-hold-what-must-be-coherent`, `rule:http-server/session-backend-is-shared-or-db-and-local-is-refused-at-boot`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The claim is about two cores, and it is pinned at the one place a program
// can be held to it without there being two: the **boot**. `rule:concurrency/the-local-tier-cannot-hold-what-must-be-coherent` makes
// `Core\Session` the one exception to the local tier, and a refusal at boot is
// what makes the property total — a fleet that never happened to be scheduled
// across cores would pass any test written from inside a request, and would
// then lose sessions in production at a rate set by the load balancer.
//
// `session-start-reaches-the-configured-shared-store-and-never-one-of-its-own`
// is the other side of the same rule, over a tree that chose a store § 3
// admits: there the member reaches `[cache.shared]` and reports it by name.
// Here the tree chooses the one store it may not, and nothing runs at all.
//
// The diagnostic's own note carries the reason rather than the case's comment
// doing it, which is why the note is asserted and not skipped past: a code
// whose text stopped saying *why* per-core storage is wrong would still refuse
// and would still leave the next reader to rediscover `rule:concurrency/the-local-tier-cannot-hold-what-must-be-coherent`.
Core\Session::start();
--FILE nvs.toml--
# The one value § 3's roster does not hold. `shared` and `db` are the two that
# survive the core that accepted the request; this is the third thing an
# operator reaches for and the reason the roster is closed.
[session]
backend = "local"
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0626]: `[session] backend = "local"` names no store a session may live in
  = note: `rule:concurrency/the-local-tier-cannot-hold-what-must-be-coherent`: a session read on one core and written on another must see one value, and the local tier is per-core%A
  = help: write `backend = `"shared"` or `"db"``
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
